module gunbc.materialization_kernel_closing_frontier_audit


data materialization_kernel_closing_frontier_audit_note: String = "RENAMED from gunbc.materialization_kernel_closing_contract (still-bat-561 operator ruling, 2026-08-02, msg_9609b3a3): this module is an AUDIT of the v1-materialization-kernel roadmap node's closing frontier, not the closing contract itself. The original framing was a DESIGN §5 violation at the architectural level — verdicts were AUTHORED (hand-written Delivered/PartiallyDelivered/NotDelivered rows with prose evidence) rather than DERIVED from executed observations, so editing a row from NotDelivered to Delivered would green the file without executing any operation the evidence string names. That is exactly the named anti-pattern: 'a check satisfiable by editing the declaration while the realizer still lies.' A genuine closing contract would need each clause to carry a typed OBSERVATION (ExecutedPass / ExecutedRefusal / Unavailable) with the verdict DERIVED from it, not authored beside it — that machinery does not exist here and this file does not claim to be that.

What this file actually is, and remains useful for (operator: 'your audit is genuinely useful and it should land; it just must not claim to be the closing mechanism'): a per-clause investigation record against the seven obligations the parent brief (still-bat-561, Lane F) named, each citing the concrete executing witness_module/witness_fn that was actually run to reach its verdict, or the concrete symbol/gap that keeps it open. The prose evidence fields are audit findings a human or a future session can verify by re-running the cited witnesses — they are not self-verifying, and this file does not claim the roadmap node's red_control or handback is satisfied by anything in it. materialization_kernel_all_clauses_delivered below is a derived SUMMARY over the audited rows (an AND-fold), not a roadmap execution contract.

Per-clause sourcing (audited 2026-08-02, session quick-swift-501, against PR #7534 as merged and the live tree, not against the PR's own prose): every Delivered/PartiallyDelivered/NotDelivered verdict below names an executing witness_module/witness_fn pair or, for NotDelivered/PartiallyDelivered, the concrete symbol whose absence or shape keeps the clause from closing. Nothing here restates std.materialization_ladder or std.materialization_provider vocabulary (DESIGN §3 single authority / the brief's 'NO SECOND CACHE MECHANISM' instruction) — this audit sits one layer above them, checking whether the v1-materialization-kernel roadmap node's OWN stated obligations are discharged by the CacheProvider/ArtifactRequest machinery those modules already define, never minting a parallel cache or provider concept.

WHAT REMAINS OUTSIDE THIS FILE'S AUTHORITY: acceptance of the roadmap node itself is a gunbc.roadmap_model RoadmapAcceptanceReceipt, authored by the operator (roadmap_acceptance_receipt_note names accepted_by as evidence, not a worker action); this audit does not accept the node and does not claim to, and it is not itself the node's closing contract. It gives a human reviewer, or a future execution-derived contract, something concrete to check against instead of prose."

type ClauseVerdict
  = NotDelivered { reason: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | PartiallyDelivered { reason: std.types.NonEmptyStr, evidence: std.types.NonEmptyStr }
  | Delivered { witness_module: std.types.NonEmptyStr, witness_fn: std.types.NonEmptyStr, evidence: std.types.NonEmptyStr }

type FrontierClause {
  id: std.types.NonEmptyStr
  statement: std.types.NonEmptyStr
  verdict: ClauseVerdict
}

data clause_delivered_note: String = "The one exhaustive match on ClauseVerdict in this module; every other Bool-producing projection on a FrontierClause routes through this (review 47530, DESIGN §3 — an undeclared sum re-matched by a family of free predicates duplicates the same exhaustiveness fact at each call site)."

fn clause_delivered(c: FrontierClause) -> Bool {
  match c.verdict {
    Delivered { witness_module: _, witness_fn: _, evidence: _ } => true
    PartiallyDelivered { reason: _, evidence: _ } => false
    NotDelivered { reason: _ } => false
  }
}

data clause_has_any_evidence_note: String = "DELETED (review 47530 round 2, still-bat-561): this module previously carried clause_has_any_evidence, a Bool-returning fn that always returned true because every ClauseVerdict variant requires a NonEmptyStr reason/evidence field by construction — the bad state (a clause with no evidence) has no constructor, so the check could not fail. A function named has_any_evidence that returns true unconditionally reads as a performed check to any caller who does not open it, which is worse than no function at all (DESIGN §4b(4) — a climb deletes the redundant lower-rung PRODUCTION machinery the construction obsoletes; §5 — a check standing where construction already makes the state unwritable is validation, not verification). materialization_kernel_every_clause_has_evidence, its sole caller, was deleted with it for the same reason, and the witness that asserted it (materialization_kernel_every_clause_carries_evidence) was deleted rather than kept green-by-tautology. This note is the surviving, durable part: every FrontierClause carries evidence because ClauseVerdict's three variants each require a NonEmptyStr field (reason, or reason+evidence, or witness_module+witness_fn+evidence) — read the type in this file if you need to confirm that property holds; there is nothing left to call."

fn closing_frontier_clauses() -> List<FrontierClause> {
  [
    FrontierClause {
      id: "contract-exists-and-can-fail",
      statement: "The v1-materialization-kernel node has an actual, checkable audit capable of failing on zero progress (brief step 1).",
      verdict: Delivered {
        witness_module: "test.claim.materialization_kernel_closing_frontier_audit_witness",
        witness_fn: "materialization_kernel_audit_not_all_delivered_today",
        evidence: "This module and its paired witness test are the audit; the fold below evaluates false against the audited clauses that follow, proving by execution that the audit summary can read false rather than vacuously passing."
      }
    },
    FrontierClause {
      id: "warm-hit-skips-semantic-recompute",
      statement: "A restart-stable exact hit skips the semantic computation the artifact claims to replace, proven by execution rather than by serving an equal result (brief step 2).",
      verdict: NotDelivered {
        reason: "REGRESSION DECLARED 2026-08-11 (gunbc#8146, review 51132). PREVIOUS RUNG: Delivered. TEMPORARY RUNG: NotDelivered. REASON: the cited witness module was executed and does not pass — resolve_cross_process_cache_test reports 53 passed / 3 FAILED (provider_disposition_four_arm_matrix, repeat_resolve_through_disk_seam_does_not_reenter_provider, same_subject_resolves_share_one_graph_store_hits_v2_disk, the last two cascading from a poisoned GUNBC_RESOLVED_GRAPH_CACHE_DIR env mutex) in 1321s. The Delivered verdict was therefore ALREADY inflated before this PR: the suite was gated by --no-run, so no run ever contradicted it. This row does not lower a real rung, it corrects a reported one to the rung executed evidence establishes (DESIGN §4b(1)). BOUNDED POPULATION: the three clauses citing resolve_cross_process_cache_test and resolved_graph_cache_size_bound_test. RESTORATION TRIGGER: root-cause and fix the failing tests, bring the module under the gate budget (22min exceeds the 15min step cap), and re-declare it in test.retirement.model — at which point the evidence executes and this clause may return to Delivered. THIS CLAUSE specifically: cross_process_hit_skips_semantic_recompute (the TYPECHECK_COMPUTE_COUNT skip proof) is not among the three failures, but it shares the poisoned env mutex and the module as a whole does not pass, so the module cannot be enrolled and the clause has no executing consumer." as std.types.NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FrontierClause {
      id: "corruption-identity-completeness-overcap-refuse",
      statement: "Corruption, wrong identity, incomplete content, and over-cap storage each refuse without cold widening (brief step 3).",
      verdict: NotDelivered {
        reason: "REGRESSION DECLARED 2026-08-11 (gunbc#8146, review 51132). PREVIOUS RUNG: Delivered. TEMPORARY RUNG: NotDelivered. REASON: the cited witness module was executed and does not pass — resolve_cross_process_cache_test reports 53 passed / 3 FAILED (provider_disposition_four_arm_matrix, repeat_resolve_through_disk_seam_does_not_reenter_provider, same_subject_resolves_share_one_graph_store_hits_v2_disk, the last two cascading from a poisoned GUNBC_RESOLVED_GRAPH_CACHE_DIR env mutex) in 1321s. The Delivered verdict was therefore ALREADY inflated before this PR: the suite was gated by --no-run, so no run ever contradicted it. This row does not lower a real rung, it corrects a reported one to the rung executed evidence establishes (DESIGN §4b(1)). BOUNDED POPULATION: the three clauses citing resolve_cross_process_cache_test and resolved_graph_cache_size_bound_test. RESTORATION TRIGGER: root-cause and fix the failing tests, bring the module under the gate budget (22min exceeds the 15min step cap), and re-declare it in test.retirement.model — at which point the evidence executes and this clause may return to Delivered. THIS CLAUSE specifically: its refusal witnesses live in the same unenrollable module; provider-grain corroboration in materialization_provider_resolved_graph_consumer_test remains retained and executing, but corroboration is not the claim." as std.types.NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FrontierClause {
      id: "bounded-eviction-and-full-store",
      statement: "Bounded-store eviction and full-store behavior are modeled and executed (brief step 4).",
      verdict: NotDelivered {
        reason: "REGRESSION DECLARED 2026-08-11 (gunbc#8146, review 51132). PREVIOUS RUNG: Delivered. TEMPORARY RUNG: NotDelivered. REASON: the cited witness module was executed and does not pass — resolve_cross_process_cache_test reports 53 passed / 3 FAILED (provider_disposition_four_arm_matrix, repeat_resolve_through_disk_seam_does_not_reenter_provider, same_subject_resolves_share_one_graph_store_hits_v2_disk, the last two cascading from a poisoned GUNBC_RESOLVED_GRAPH_CACHE_DIR env mutex) in 1321s. The Delivered verdict was therefore ALREADY inflated before this PR: the suite was gated by --no-run, so no run ever contradicted it. This row does not lower a real rung, it corrects a reported one to the rung executed evidence establishes (DESIGN §4b(1)). BOUNDED POPULATION: the three clauses citing resolve_cross_process_cache_test and resolved_graph_cache_size_bound_test. RESTORATION TRIGGER: root-cause and fix the failing tests, bring the module under the gate budget (22min exceeds the 15min step cap), and re-declare it in test.retirement.model — at which point the evidence executes and this clause may return to Delivered. THIS CLAUSE specifically: resolved_graph_cache_size_bound_test is deleted with the failing sibling it shares a lane with; its own two tests were not observed failing, and it is deleted for lack of a consumer rather than for failing." as std.types.NonEmptyStr
      }
    },
    FrontierClause {
      id: "lookup-ahead-of-index-construction",
      statement: "Lookup moves ahead of index construction, and only after the identity and refusal contract from the two clauses above is preserved at the new position (brief step 5).",
      verdict: NotDelivered {
        reason: "GATE RE-CLOSED 2026-08-11 (gunbc#8146, review 51190). This reason previously read that the warm-hit-skips-semantic-recompute gate was lifted because that clause had reached Delivered — true when written, falsified in this same PR when that clause was demoted to NotDelivered on the measurement that its cited witness module fails (53 pass / 3 fail / 1321s) and had never executed under --no-run. So step 5 is BLOCKED again, not honestly unstarted: its prerequisite is back to NotDelivered and re-opens with it. The underlying code position is unchanged either way: v1_compiler.cli_run fn resolved_graph_from_sources_with_index's cross-process probe still runs after process_shared_index and entry-closure/source loading, unchanged from PR #7534's own self-documented scope limit ('this does not close dashboard startup ... a warm hit skips typecheck/reconcile but still pays corpus-index/source-loading')."
      }
    },
    FrontierClause {
      id: "real-production-invocation",
      statement: "One real production invocation is bound; an opt-in test-only environment variable is not completion (brief step 6).",
      verdict: NotDelivered {
        reason: "The only enabled route remains the opt-in GUNBC_RESOLVED_GRAPH_CACHE_DIR environment variable, read by v1_compiler.cli_run fn resolved_graph_cache_root_from_env and guarded by cross_process_provider_routing_suppressed. The in-tree comment on resolved_graph_from_sources_with_index states floor and CI leave it unset and only explicit test harnesses arm the disk tier; no default CI job, dashboard serve path, or product build sets it today."
      }
    },
    FrontierClause {
      id: "hand-rust-growth-tracked-live",
      statement: "The recorded hand-Rust growth and its deletion trigger stay live until the host bridge is emitted or removed (brief step 7).",
      verdict: Delivered {
        witness_module: "test.claim.resolved_graph_cache_hand_rust_witness",
        witness_fn: "resolved_graph_cache_hand_rust_receipt_is_checkable",
        evidence: "UPDATED 2026-08-11 (gunbc#8146, review 51152): the population shrank with the test-suite cutover and this prose is corrected to the live figures rather than left describing a tree that no longer exists. gunbc.resolved_graph_cache_hand_rust_scaffold now enrolls FOUR touched paths (v1_compiler.cli_run; v1_compiler.cli_run.materialization_provider_consumer; v1_compiler.resolved_graph_cache; materialization_provider_resolved_graph_consumer_test.rs) with per-path net LOC deltas summing to 1256. Three of the original seven departed with the cutover: ir_fixture_seam_soundness_test.rs, resolve_cross_process_cache_test.rs and resolved_graph_cache_size_bound_test.rs. THE CLAUSE STAYS Delivered, and its evidence is STRONGER than before, which is why: resolved_graph_cache_hand_rust_receipt_is_checkable no longer checks only a list length and a LOC fold — it now joins every censused path to a readable file (every_censused_path_exists), so a path deleted out from under this receipt refuses instead of passing. That join is what caught this drift. Both the primary scaffold and the paired gunbc.materialization_provider_consumer_scaffold remain std.disposition Scaffold\{dissolves_to: SingleAuthority\} (seed-retained, named dissolve trigger: cli_run_hollowing_plan area 2.6 typed module cache/memo, or witness-realization landing a typed host-effect transport), never silently absorbed as permanent."
      }
    },
  ]
}

fn materialization_kernel_progress_count(clauses: List<FrontierClause>) -> Int {
  clauses |> filter(c => clause_delivered(c: c)) |> count()
}

fn materialization_kernel_clause_count(clauses: List<FrontierClause>) -> Int {
  count(clauses)
}

data materialization_kernel_all_clauses_delivered_note: String = "RENAMED from materialization_kernel_closing_contract_holds (still-bat-561 operator ruling, 2026-08-02): this is a derived AUDIT SUMMARY over closing_frontier_clauses — true only if every audited clause independently reached Delivered — not a roadmap execution contract and not itself bound to the v1-materialization-kernel roadmap node's acceptance. See materialization_kernel_closing_frontier_audit_note above for why the prior framing (an authored AND-fold presented as 'the contract') was retired."

fn materialization_kernel_all_clauses_delivered(clauses: List<FrontierClause>) -> Bool {
  clauses |> fold(init: true, f: (acc, c) => acc && clause_delivered(c: c))
}
